{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Extensions"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A type’s own page lists only the members of its own module. Each page here collects the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"members that every other module adds to one type."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedGraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedHypergraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-Graph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-Hypergraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableGraph-Extensions"],"anchor":"GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule-DirectedAcyclicGraph-Extensions"],"anchor":"DirectedAcyclicGraphModule","title":"DirectedAcyclicGraphModule"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Forest-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions","doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Tree-Extensions"],"anchor":"Trees","title":"Trees"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/BipartiteGraphs-BipartiteGraph-Extensions"],"anchor":"BipartiteGraphs","title":"BipartiteGraphs"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The members each module adds to types declared in another module, by extended type."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"Grafluent"}],"title":"Extensions Across Modules"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluent\/extensions"]}],"references":{"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-Hypergraph-Extensions":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-Hypergraph-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-hypergraph-extensions","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Extensions to Hypergraph","type":"topic"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Edmonds). A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent (zero or one), and each edge is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arborescence"}],"title":"Arborescence","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arborescence"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Extensions to MutableDirectedGraph","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-mutabledirectedgraph-extensions"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Kept apart","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"go forward.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph"},"doc://DirectedAcyclicGraphModule/documentation/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule/DirectedAcyclicGraph":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/DirectedAcyclicGraph","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/directedacyclicgraphmodule\/directedacyclicgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph with no directed cycle, which keeps a topological order of its vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"current as it changes (JGraphT’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", petgraph’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"acyclic::Acyclic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"MutableGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" concept","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"add_vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"add_edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove_edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove_vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a "},{"code":"Tree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be mutated."}],"title":"Tree","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tree"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph that generic code can fill: the undirected counterpart of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" concept, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"type":"text","text":"), with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"members a reader needs to build a graph by key."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MutableGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutablegraph"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-RootedTree-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-rootedtree-extensions","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Extensions to RootedTree"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directedView"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"title":"Graph","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}]},"doc://BipartiteGraphs/documentation/BipartiteGraphs/BipartiteGraph":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BipartiteGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/BipartiteGraphs\/documentation\/BipartiteGraphs\/BipartiteGraph","url":"\/documentation\/bipartitegraphs\/bipartitegraph","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph with two fixed sides, every edge joining a left vertex to a right vertex, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no self-loop. Simple: an edge is inserted once, in either orientation. Each edge is stored left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"endpoint first, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[e].u"},{"type":"text","text":" is its left end."}],"title":"BipartiteGraph","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BipartiteGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-DirectedGraph-Extensions":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-directedgraph-extensions","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-DirectedGraph-Extensions","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Extensions to DirectedGraph","type":"topic"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"A generic, high-performance graph library for Swift.","type":"text"}],"title":"Grafluent","type":"topic"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Forest":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Forest","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A forest: an acyclic undirected graph, possibly empty, so a disjoint union of trees (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isolated vertex is a one-vertex tree). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trees"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them by least vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" says which one a vertex is in."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Forest"}],"title":"Forest","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Forest"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/forest"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-BidirectionalDi